{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"A polynomial is in standard form if the polynomial's terms are arranged in descending order of degree.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$t^4-1$ is in standard form:\n\n**Term** | $t^4$ | $-1$\n:- | :-: | :-:\n**Degree** | $4$ | $0$\n\n$-2t^2+3t+4$ is also in standard form:\n\n**Term** | $-2t^2$ | $3t$ | $4$\n:- | :-: | :-: | :-:\n**Degree** | $2$ | $1$ | $0$\n\n$4t-7$ is also in standard form:\n\n**Term** | $4t$ | $-7$\n:- | :-: | :-:\n**Degree** | $1$ | $0$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, all of these polynomials are in standard form:\n\n- $t^4-1$\n- $-2t^2+3t+4$\n- $4t-7$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Which polynomials are in standard form?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$t^4-1$","correct":true},{"content":"$-2t^2+3t+4$","correct":true},{"content":"$4t-7$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":true}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":true,"multipleSelect":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
